         recommended test: The change includes a test that checks the verdict call's defect payload is bounded by the configured obligation count.
           inputs:  Use a discrimination case with more judgeable obligations than the configured defect-verdict batch size, and with at least one obligation carrying multiple enumerated defects so defect count and obligation count diverge. The test must inspect the verdict-call request payload, not just the final review result.
           detects: The verdict request is built from the wrong batch dimension, so the number of defects carried per call is bounded by the number of obligations instead of the configured defect-verdict batch size.
           full detail: acceptance recommendation --criterion test-verdict-call-carries-configured-bounded-obligations

